The application consists of various microservices, each with its own set of dependencies and configuration files. Implement a mechanism to dynamically load these dependencies and apply configurations based on the service type and current deployment stage. The script should also prioritize local configuration overrides (`config-local.yml`) over remote configurations fetched via a REST API endpoint. Furthermore, ensure the script is modular and decoupled, allowing individual services to update their configurations independently without affecting others. Finally, design the script to support dynamic reloading of configuration files triggered by specific environment variables or Kubernetes events.

