This code defines a Node.js-based CI/CD pipeline that automates the deployment of a microservices application across multiple environments. The pipeline uses GitHub as its source control system, Docker for container image management, Kubernetes for cluster orchestration, and Jenkins for CI/CD automation.

The pipeline is triggered by GitHub push events, pull requests, and scheduled tasks. It has three stages: Build, Test, and Deploy. The Build stage installs dependencies and builds the microservices application using Docker. The Test stage runs integration tests using Jest. The Deploy stage deploys the microservices application to each environment (development, testing, staging) using Docker.

The pipeline also includes monitoring and logging using Prometheus, Grafana, and custom logging. It uses a sophisticated dependency resolution system to handle circular dependencies and complex service interdependencies within the microservices architecture.

