Here is the PHP code for the `updateClinicStatus` function:

```php
<?php
require_once 'config.php';
require_once 'redis_client.php';

function updateClinicStatus($clinic_id, $new_status, $last_modified_ip) {
    try {
        // Establish a connection to the database
        $db = new PDO('mysql:host=' . DB_HOST . ';dbname=' . DB_NAME, DB_USER, DB_PASSWORD);

        // Set the charset and error mode
        $db->setAttribute(PDO::ATTR_ERRMODE, PDO::ERRMODE_EXCEPTION);
        $db->exec("SET NAMES 'utf8'");

        // Prepare a transaction to update the clinic status
        $transaction = $db->beginTransaction();

        try {
            // Update the clinic status using prepared statements
            $stmt = $db->prepare("UPDATE clinics SET status = :new_status, last_modified_ip = :last_modified_ip, last_modified_date = NOW() WHERE id = :clinic_id");
            $stmt->execute([':new_status' => $new_status, ':last_modified_ip' => $last_modified_ip, ':clinic_id' => $clinic_id]);

            // Commit the transaction
            $transaction->commit();
        } catch (Exception $e) {
            // Rollback the transaction if an error occurs during update
            $transaction->rollback();

            // Log the error to the monitoring service
            logErrorToMonitoringService($e, $clinic_id);
        }
    } catch (PDOException $e) {
        // Log the database error to the monitoring service
        logErrorToMonitoringService($e, $clinic_id);

        // Handle the error if the update fails due to a database issue
        handleDatabaseError($e, $clinic_id);
    }

    // Implement rate limiter using Redis
    $redis = new RedisClient();
    $rate_limiter_key = 'update_clinic_status_rate_limit';
    $recent_updates = $redis->hgetall($rate_limiter_key);

    if (isset($recent_updates[$last_modified_ip])) {
        $update_count = $recent_updates[$last_modified_ip] + 1;

        // Check if the rate limit has been exceeded
        if ($update_count > 5) {
            // Return an error message if the rate limit is exceeded
            return 'Rate limit exceeded';
        } else {
            // Update the Redis cache with the new update count
            $redis->hset($rate_limiter_key, $last_modified_ip, $update_count);
        }
    } else {
        // Initialize the Redis cache for this IP address
        $redis->hset($rate_limiter_key, $last_modified_ip, 1);
    }

    // Return a success message if the update is successful
    return 'Update successful';
}

// Helper function to log errors to the monitoring service
function logErrorToMonitoringService(Exception $e, $clinic_id) {
    // Implement error logging using Prometheus or Grafana
    echo 'Error logged: ' . $e->getMessage() . "\n";
}

// Helper function to handle database errors during update
function handleDatabaseError(PDOException $e, $clinic_id) {
    // Implement error handling for database issues
    echo 'Database error: ' . $e->getMessage() . "\n";
}
```

Note that this code assumes you have a `config.php` file with database credentials and a `redis_client.php` file to establish a connection to Redis. You'll need to implement the error logging and handling functions as well as the rate limiter logic according to your specific requirements.

